T*
() Tj
T*
(- id: H-NM-01; name: Focus Question First; when: Starting ANY concept mapping activity; rule: Always) Tj
T*
(begin with a clear focus question: 'What are the key concepts in {domain}?' or 'How does {concept_A}) Tj
T*
(relate to {concept_B}?'. The focus question constrains the map and prevents scope creep.; severity:) Tj
T*
(MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-NM-02; name: Hierarchical Ordering; when: Arranging concepts on the map; rule: Place most) Tj
T*
(general/inclusive concepts at top, most specific at bottom. Maximum 5 levels. If you have more than 5) Tj
T*
(levels, the domain needs to be split into sub-domains.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-NM-03; name: Cross-Link Minimum; when: Completing any concept map; rule: Every concept map must) Tj
T*
(have at least 3 cross-links between different branches. Cross-links are the most valuable part of the map) Tj
T*
(? they show integrative understanding. Fewer than 3 = shallow map.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-NM-04; name: 5-Curricula Minimum; when: Comparing existing curricula for a domain; rule: Compare) Tj
T*
(minimum 5 existing curricula before designing new. If fewer than 5 found, WARN the user that the) Tj
T*
(comparison base is insufficient and results may be biased. FALLBACK for 2-3 curricula found: WARN and) Tj
T*
(present options: \(1\) Accept reduced comparison with caveats, \(2\) Request SME interviews to supplement) Tj
T*
(research, \(3\) Expand search to adjacent domains for broader context.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
ET
