T*
(- Mapeamento e melhoria de processos) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Heursticas relevantes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-01; name: Review First, Always; when: Starting any lesson design; rule: EVERY lesson starts) Tj
T*
(with retrieval of previous content \(Principle 1\). Not a summary, not a 're-read your notes' ? actual) Tj
T*
(retrieval practice where learners must recall from memory. If the lesson is the first in a course, review) Tj
T*
(prerequisite knowledge instead.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-02; name: Small Steps Enforcement; when: Presenting new material; rule: New material must be) Tj
T*
(in SMALL STEPS ? maximum 1-2 new concepts per step \(Principle 2\). After each step, there must be a) Tj
T*
(practice opportunity or comprehension check. Never present more than 10 minutes of new content without a) Tj
T*
(check.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-03; name: Specific Questions Only; when: Checking for understanding; rule: Never use 'Any) Tj
T*
(questions?' or 'Does everyone understand?' ? these are useless \(Principles 3, 6\). Use specific questions) Tj
T*
(that require demonstrating understanding: 'What would happen if...?', 'How is X different from Y?',) Tj
T*
('Solve this problem...'; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-04; name: Model Before Practice; when: Introducing a new skill or procedure; rule: Always show) Tj
T*
(a worked example BEFORE asking learners to practice \(Principle 4\). The worked example must show the) Tj
T*
(process step by step with explicit reasoning. Expert blind spot: if you can do it automatically, you MUST) Tj
T*
(slow down and show every step.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-05; name: Guided ? Independent Progression; when: Designing practice activities; rule:) Tj
T*
(Practice must progress from guided \(with support\) to independent \(without support\) \(Principles 5, 9\).) Tj
T*
(Never jump from instruction to independent practice ? always include guided practice as a bridge.;) Tj
T*
(severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
ET
