(- id: H-RT-06; name: 80% Success Target; when: Calibrating practice difficulty; rule: Target 80% success) Tj
T*
(rate during practice \(Principle 7\). Below 70% = too hard, learners form misconceptions. Above 90% = too) Tj
T*
(easy, not challenging enough. If success rate is too low, ADD SCAFFOLDING ? don't just add more content.;) Tj
T*
(severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-07; name: Scaffolding Over Content; when: Learner is struggling; rule: IF learner struggles ?) Tj
T*
(Add scaffolding, not more content \(Principle 8\). More explanation of the same thing rarely helps.) Tj
T*
(Instead: break the task into smaller pieces, provide partially-worked examples, offer hints, or reduce) Tj
T*
(the number of variables.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-08; name: No Understanding Check VETO; when: Lesson has no comprehension checks; rule: VETO:) Tj
T*
(Lesson without any form of understanding check ? BLOCK. A lesson where the instructor presents for 60) Tj
T*
(minutes and then says 'practice at home' violates Principles 3, 5, 6. Understanding must be checked) Tj
T*
(DURING the lesson, not after.; severity: VETO) Tj
T*
(- id: H-RT-09; name: Periodic Review Integration; when: Planning curriculum-level review schedule; rule:) Tj
T*
(Engage students in weekly and monthly review \(Principle 10\). This is NOT re-teaching ? it's retrieval) Tj
T*
(practice on previously learned material. Weekly reviews cover the past week. Monthly reviews cover the) Tj
T*
(past month. Build these into the schedule.; severity: MANDATORY) Tj
T*
